==English==
{{wikipedia|Adam's ale}}

===Etymology===
Attested 1643.<ref>{{R:Phrase Finder|entry=Adam’s ale|url=http://www.phrases.org.uk/meanings/24300.html|accessdate=26 February 2017}}</ref> Reference to the only drink available to [[Adam]], the first man in the biblical tradition, while in [[Eden]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[Adam]][['s]] [[ale]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|humorous|idiom}} [[water#Noun|Water]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Adam's wine}}
#* {{RQ:Prynne Soveraigne Power|part=2|page=32|passage=[T]hey have beene ''ſhut up in priſons and dungeons'' lying on the cold ground, ſtones or boards without beds, ſtraw, fire or any the leaſt refreſhment; allowed onely a poore pittance of '''''Adams'' Ale''', and ſcarce a penny bread a day to ſupport their lives, though their friends would provide it for them; [...]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017 |title=Decline and Fall on Savage Street|author=Fiona Farrell|page=59 |ISBN=9780143770633|passage=She had loaded Floss into the basket, tied a sugarbag containing necessities—sketch pad, pencils, corned beef sandwiches wrapped in newsprint, a bottle of water from the garden tap, the best water, the clearest, '''Adam's ale''' — to the frame of her bicycle and set off, Floss sits up in the basket, looking ahead, though of course she can't see, but her nose is up, her world a dizzy palette of smell, as clear and bright as it is to Sybil, pedalling carefully along the river and down Fitzgerald Avenue towards the hills.}}

